process-schedule.m's scheduler spawned on the machine's GPU (docs/INPROGRESS.md,
GPU processes that run loops): its loops under schedule(dynamic) run across
every team of its module's kernel that no process uses, each thread claiming
its iterations from the loop's claims word with one atomic add a wave, and
its team loop's threads from the word in the team's local memory.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-schedule.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-schedule.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

Without -fopenmp the directives are comments, and the scheduler runs its
loops itself, one iteration after another.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-schedule.m -o %t.sequential
RUN: %gpu-env %t.sequential gpu | FileCheck %S/process-schedule.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

What the loops' bodies made goes with the scheduler's arena when it ends.
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FREED
FREED: Merkurius runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
FREED-NEXT: Merkurius runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
